[{:db/id 17592186147482 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f69f8dbf-c5fe-511e-99d9-e38d8cf15603" "question-531b238d-9ec5-5151-9050-8a13d6c81fc4" "question-9c992df1-7527-5704-a514-e6a1af6606d9" "question-57978705-e111-53de-8645-669c0f65f078" "question-0a2a2098-138e-50a0-bcab-3c6c1a13bf55"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147162 :question/problem "What is $4 \\%$ of $35?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}=  \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $35$, and the percentage is $4 \\%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n4 \\% = 4 \\div 100 = 0.04\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =4%\\times 35 \\\\  & =0.04\\times 35 \\\\  & =1.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4 \\%$ of $35$ is $1.4.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n4 \\% = \\dfrac{4}{100}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =4%\\times 35 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{100}\\times 35 \\\\  & =\\frac{140}{100} \\\\  & =1.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $4 \\%$ of $35$ is $1.4.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147483 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b63c78ef-ce78-5787-b3da-65a5a527693b" "question-28285ccd-1dac-57e7-a3e5-0e93bbb0a6e3" "question-e7f35be5-687e-57cd-bcc5-6295920b0ded" "question-73c0aa3a-243e-5963-842c-b0c9efdd1ff7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147163 :question/problem "What is $140 \\%$ of $30?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}=  \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $30$, and the percentage is $140\\%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n140 \\% = 140 \\div 100 = 1.4\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140%\\times 30 \\\\  & =1.4\\times 30 \\\\  & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140 \\%$ of $30$ is $42.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n140 \\% = \\dfrac{140}{100} = \\dfrac{140 \\div 20}{100\\div 20} = \\dfrac{7}{5}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =140%\\times 30 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{5}\\times 30 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{30}{5} \\\\  & =7\\times 6 \\\\  & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $140 \\%$ of $30$ is $42.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147484 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-41c7e58b-9463-581a-ad4d-8589209fcfa8" "question-338475e3-69eb-591d-aac8-e4880e67ce0d" "question-760d2db7-2400-527c-8dd9-416b456caf4a" "question-91d7c0f9-d7dc-529a-84d9-52cae01b410f" "question-e6cea0e8-6d8a-5845-b043-a8160aa27bec"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147164 :question/problem "What is $3.6 \\%$ of $25?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part}=  \\textrm{percentage}\\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $25$, and the percentage is $3.6 \\%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n3.6 \\% = 3.6 \\div 100 = 0.036\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =3.6%\\times 25 \\\\  & =0.036\\times 25 \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3.6 \\%$ of $25$ is $0.9.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n3.6 \\% = \\dfrac{3.6}{100} = \\dfrac{3.6 \\times 10}{100 \\times 10} = \\dfrac{36}{1,000}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =3.6%\\times 25 \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{1,000}\\times 25 \\\\  & =\\frac{900}{1,000} \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $3.6 \\%$ of $25$ is $0.9.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-f69f8dbf-c5fe-511e-99d9-e38d8cf15603" :question/id #uuid "f69f8dbf-c5fe-511e-99d9-e38d8cf15603" :question/math-academy-id "q-186013" :question/problem "$16%$ of $75$ is equal to{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $75,$ and the percentage is $16%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n16%=16÷100=0.16\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =16%\\times 75 \\\\  & =0.16\\times 75 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $16%$ of $75$ is $12.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n16%=\\frac{16}{100}=\\frac{16÷4}{100÷4}=\\frac{4}{25}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =16%\\times 75 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{25}\\times 75 \\\\  & =4\\times \\frac{75}{25} \\\\  & =4\\times 3 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $16%$ of $75$ is $12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-27144d86-d03b-56ba-a1e7-6e8140f4f00d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-27144d86-d03b-56ba-a1e7-6e8140f4f00d" :answer-field/id #uuid "27144d86-d03b-56ba-a1e7-6e8140f4f00d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6ec249ec-1e7d-5f1d-8481-0bff2033980f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6ec249ec-1e7d-5f1d-8481-0bff2033980f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6ec249ec-1e7d-5f1d-8481-0bff2033980f" :answer/id #uuid "6ec249ec-1e7d-5f1d-8481-0bff2033980f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-531b238d-9ec5-5151-9050-8a13d6c81fc4" :question/id #uuid "531b238d-9ec5-5151-9050-8a13d6c81fc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-186001" :question/problem "$45%$ of $120$ is equal to{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $120,$ and the percentage is $45%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n45%=45÷100=0.45\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =45%\\times 120 \\\\  & =0.45\\times 120 \\\\  & =54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $45%$ of $120$ is $54.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n45%=\\frac{45}{100}=\\frac{45÷5}{100÷5}=\\frac{9}{20}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =45%\\times 120 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{20}\\times 120 \\\\  & =9\\times \\frac{120}{20} \\\\  & =9\\times 6 \\\\  & =54\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $45%$ of $120$ is $54.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f9d7c0cc-a432-5dde-b218-23194c823777"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f9d7c0cc-a432-5dde-b218-23194c823777" :answer-field/id #uuid "f9d7c0cc-a432-5dde-b218-23194c823777" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-60147acb-712b-5bd9-8b4c-f0e8e4cc4a6a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-60147acb-712b-5bd9-8b4c-f0e8e4cc4a6a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60147acb-712b-5bd9-8b4c-f0e8e4cc4a6a" :answer/id #uuid "60147acb-712b-5bd9-8b4c-f0e8e4cc4a6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "54" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9c992df1-7527-5704-a514-e6a1af6606d9" :question/id #uuid "9c992df1-7527-5704-a514-e6a1af6606d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-186017" :question/problem "$7%$ of $500$ is equal to{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $500,$ and the percentage is $7%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n7%=7÷100=0.07\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =7%\\times 500 \\\\  & =0.07\\times 500 \\\\  & =35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7%$ of $500$ is $35.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n7%=\\frac{7}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =7%\\times 500 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{100}\\times 500 \\\\  & =7\\times \\frac{500}{100} \\\\  & =7\\times 5 \\\\  & =35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $7%$ of $500$ is $35.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5b936e0f-a046-500e-a716-4e3ada6e006f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5b936e0f-a046-500e-a716-4e3ada6e006f" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b936e0f-a046-500e-a716-4e3ada6e006f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-61af182a-8c1c-5ca5-8a5d-09d3e8efd6fd" :answer-field/choices ["answer-61af182a-8c1c-5ca5-8a5d-09d3e8efd6fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61af182a-8c1c-5ca5-8a5d-09d3e8efd6fd" :answer/id #uuid "61af182a-8c1c-5ca5-8a5d-09d3e8efd6fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "35" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-57978705-e111-53de-8645-669c0f65f078" :question/id #uuid "57978705-e111-53de-8645-669c0f65f078" :question/math-academy-id "q-61521" :question/problem "What is $9%$ of $1,000?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $1,000$, and the percentage is $9%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n9%=9÷100=0.09\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =9%\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =0.09\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $9%$ of $1,000$ is $90.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n9%=\\frac{9}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =9%\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{100}\\times 1,000 \\\\  & =9\\times \\frac{1,000}{100} \\\\  & =9\\times 10 \\\\  & =90\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $9%$ of $1,000$ is $90.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9297761d-52d2-55ad-bbf4-4aa8059fd778"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9297761d-52d2-55ad-bbf4-4aa8059fd778" :answer-field/id #uuid "9297761d-52d2-55ad-bbf4-4aa8059fd778" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3c1f2219-22b2-54a4-bed8-e31898300102" :answer-field/choices ["answer-11421dbe-1fb6-5598-a5a3-7680bd0658a8" "answer-c79775ee-53c7-5b33-a175-3da2f6cd1630" "answer-3c1f2219-22b2-54a4-bed8-e31898300102" "answer-5fb0d6c4-1371-5cca-860b-1f75bfbf1dd8" "answer-e7ec2e86-d0cb-5742-9317-e2c8f37c781d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-11421dbe-1fb6-5598-a5a3-7680bd0658a8" :answer/id #uuid "11421dbe-1fb6-5598-a5a3-7680bd0658a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "100" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c79775ee-53c7-5b33-a175-3da2f6cd1630" :answer/id #uuid "c