{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =120%\\times 25 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}\\times 25 \\\\  & =6\\times \\frac{25}{5} \\\\  & =6\\times 5 \\\\  & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $120%$ of $25$ is $30.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186145094 :answer-field/correct 17592186145098 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-73c0aa3a-243e-5963-842c-b0c9efdd1ff7" :question/id #uuid "73c0aa3a-243e-5963-842c-b0c9efdd1ff7" :question/math-academy-id "q-186030" :question/problem "$240%$ of $50$ is equal to{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $50,$ and the percentage is $240%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n240%=240÷100=2.4\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =240%\\times 50 \\\\  & =2.4\\times 50 \\\\  & =120\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $240%$ of $50$ is $120.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n240%=\\frac{240}{100}=\\frac{240÷20}{100÷20}=\\frac{12}{5}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =240%\\times 50 \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}\\times 50 \\\\  & =12\\times \\frac{50}{5} \\\\  & =12\\times 10 \\\\  & =120\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $240%$ of $50$ is $120.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b5b4bd7-3b85-553f-bed6-89d0cab4b1a1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b5b4bd7-3b85-553f-bed6-89d0cab4b1a1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b5b4bd7-3b85-553f-bed6-89d0cab4b1a1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-6f6b2011-447f-54b2-a572-df3151a7f05c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6f6b2011-447f-54b2-a572-df3151a7f05c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f6b2011-447f-54b2-a572-df3151a7f05c" :answer/id #uuid "6f6b2011-447f-54b2-a572-df3151a7f05c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-41c7e58b-9463-581a-ad4d-8589209fcfa8" :question/id #uuid "41c7e58b-9463-581a-ad4d-8589209fcfa8" :question/math-academy-id "q-160856" :question/problem "What is $0.4%$ of $150?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $150,$ and the percentage is $0.4%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n0.4%=0.4÷100=0.004\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4%\\times 150 \\\\  & =0.004\\times 150 \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4%$ of $150$ is $0.6.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n0.4%=\\frac{0.4}{100}=\\frac{0.4\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{4}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4%\\times 150 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1,000}\\times 150 \\\\  & =\\frac{600}{1,000} \\\\  & =0.6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4%$ of $150$ is $0.6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-0495fce3-5e30-538c-9858-e374c612f1de"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-0495fce3-5e30-538c-9858-e374c612f1de" :answer-field/id #uuid "0495fce3-5e30-538c-9858-e374c612f1de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9087d490-4c3d-5031-987f-33fb68a2fb29" :answer-field/choices ["answer-39f57abf-84f0-5cf5-89fc-da5c8c9da016" "answer-f5355f84-24