ac{0.4}{100}=\\frac{0.4\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{4}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.4%\\times 750 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{1,000}\\times 750 \\\\  & =\\frac{3,000}{1,000} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.4%$ of $750$ is $3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-16a584d9-8da8-58a7-8608-91d1146e977f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-16a584d9-8da8-58a7-8608-91d1146e977f" :answer-field/id #uuid "16a584d9-8da8-58a7-8608-91d1146e977f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-ce900006-c571-5d1a-8205-026be13ff645" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ce900006-c571-5d1a-8205-026be13ff645"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ce900006-c571-5d1a-8205-026be13ff645" :answer/id #uuid "ce900006-c571-5d1a-8205-026be13ff645" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-760d2db7-2400-527c-8dd9-416b456caf4a" :question/id #uuid "760d2db7-2400-527c-8dd9-416b456caf4a" :question/math-academy-id "q-186071" :question/problem "$0.6%$ of $25$ is equal to{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $25,$ and the percentage is $0.6%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n0.6%=0.6÷100=0.006\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.6%\\times 25 \\\\  & =0.006\\times 25 \\\\  & =0.15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.6%$ of $25$ is $0.15.$ \n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n0.6%=\\frac{0.6}{100}=\\frac{0.6\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{6}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.6%\\times 25 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{1,000}\\times 25 \\\\  & =\\frac{150}{1,000} \\\\  & =0.15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.6%$ of $25$ is $0.15.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-61534651-a815-57f0-8cf9-1b460e173330"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-61534651-a815-57f0-8cf9-1b460e173330" :answer-field/id #uuid "61534651-a815-57f0-8cf9-1b460e173330" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-31e08bb2-2859-599b-82e3-db2faad45861" :answer-field/choices ["answer-31e08bb2-2859-599b-82e3-db2faad45861"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-31e08bb2-2859-599b-82e3-db2faad45861" :answer/id #uuid "31e08bb2-2859-599b-82e3-db2faad45861" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-91d7c0f9-d7dc-529a-84d9-52cae01b410f" :question/id #uuid "91d7c0f9-d7dc-529a-84d9-52cae01b410f" :question/math-academy-id "q-160859" :question/problem "What is $0.25%$ of $400?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $400,$ and the percentage is $0.25%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n0.25%=0.25÷100=0.0025\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.25%\\times 400 \\\\  & =0.0025\\times 400 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.25%$ of $400$ is $1.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n0.25%=\\frac{0.25}{100}=\\frac{0.25\\times 100}{100\\times 100}=\\frac{25}{10,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =0.25%\\times 400 \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{10,000}\\times 400 \\\\  & =\\frac{10,000}{10,000} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $0.25%$ of $400$ is $1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-86b60ba2-2790-559a-9637-46791c78910f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-86b60ba2-2790-559a-9637-46791c78910f" :answer-field/id #uuid "86b60ba2-2790-559a-9637-46791c78910f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6c239089-9b3b-5b6e-9a2a-29cb0f5b6d5d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-db71a8a8-0d3a-5054-8025-613a094f0cd0" "answer-6c239089-9b3b-5b6e-9a2a-29cb0f5b6d5d" "answer-fa0036d8-b66f-5a31-96bb-ab88630d96e4" "answer-d157906d-c910-5bc1-8716-5b2bd5c9c021" "answer-a57a33d2-a0d9-542c-88ae-e5612d73beb2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db71a8a8-0d3a-5054-8025-613a094f0cd0" :answer/id #uuid "db71a8a8-0d3a-5054-8025-613a094f0cd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6c239089-9b3b-5b6e-9a2a-29cb0f5b6d5d" :answer/id #uuid "6c239089-9b3b-5b6e-9a2a-29cb0f5b6d5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa0036d8-b66f-5a31-96bb-ab88630d96e4" :answer/id #uuid "fa0036d8-b66f-5a31-96bb-ab88630d96e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d157906d-c910-5bc1-8716-5b2bd5c9c021" :answer/id #uuid "d157906d-c910-5bc1-8716-5b2bd5c9c021" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a57a33d2-a0d9-542c-88ae-e5612d73beb2" :answer/id #uuid "a57a33d2-a0d9-542c-88ae-e5612d73beb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e6cea0e8-6d8a-5845-b043-a8160aa27bec" :question/id #uuid "e6cea0e8-6d8a-5845-b043-a8160aa27bec" :question/math-academy-id "q-160849" :question/problem "What is $1.5%$ of $60?$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is $60,$ and the percentage is $1.5%.$ \n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n1.5%=1.5÷100=0.015\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =1.5%\\times 60 \\\\  & =0.015\\times 60 \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $1.5%$ of $60$ is $0.9.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n1.5%=\\frac{1.5}{100}=\\frac{1.5\\times 10}{100\\times 10}=\\frac{15}{1,000}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =1.5%\\times 60 \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{1,000}\\times 60 \\\\  & =\\frac{900}{1,000} \\\\  & =0.9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $1.5%$ of $60$ is $0.9.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8de07806-3226-599c-87f5-c4c81b05f738"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8de07806-3226-599c-87f5-c4c81b05f738" :answer-field/id #uuid "8de07806-3226-599c-87f5-c4c81b05f738" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-49815158-cf3c-5be2-bbf6-84c56f3c9324" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6f959ade-dcdc-51d1-a2b9-989b6e916e24" "answer-222d960a-6b24-52cb-a7d5-6b9ae0042537" "answer-a6db3596-f288-520e-8011-17f3adc2e5f1" "answer-49815158-cf3c-5be2-bbf6-84c56f3c9324" "answer-4af2add2-4118-5742-aa05-3f2a4eaf1c4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f959ade-dcdc-51d1-a2b9-989b6e916e24" :answer/id #uuid "6f959ade-dcdc-51d1-a2b9-989b6e916e24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-222d960a-6b24-52cb-a7d5-6b9ae0042537" :answer/id #uuid "222d960a-6b24-52cb-a7d5-6b9ae0042537" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6db3596-f288-520e-8011-17f3adc2e5f1" :answer/id #uuid "a6db3596-f288-520e-8011-17f3adc2e5f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-49815158-cf3c-5be2-bbf6-84c56f3c9324" :answer/id #uuid "49815158-cf3c-5be2-bbf6-84c56f3c9324" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4af2add2-4118-5742-aa05-3f2a4eaf1c4c" :answer/id #uuid "4af2add2-4118-5742-aa05-3f2a4eaf1c4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186148789 :tutorial/content "We can find a percentage part of a number using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part} = \\textrm{percentage} \\times \\textrm{whole}\n$$\n\nTo illustrate, let's calculate $16 \\%$ of $300.$\n\nHere, the whole is $300$ and the percentage is $16 \\% .$ So, the part is given by\n\n$$\n\\textrm{part} = 16\\% \\times 300.\n$$\n\nBut how do we multiply a percentage by a number? We have two methods of doing this. Let's apply both and check that they give the same answer.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n16\\% = 16 \\div 100 = 0.16\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =16%\\times 300 \\\\  & =0.16\\times 300 \\\\  & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $16\\%$ of $300$ is $48.$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n16\\% = \\dfrac{16}{100}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply our formula as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =16%\\times 300 \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{100}\\times 300 \\\\  & =16\\times \\frac{300}{100} \\\\  & =16\\times 3 \\\\  & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $16 \\%$ of $300$ is $48.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186147654 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
